#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

bc_client_t *bc_connect_fd(int fd);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a client handle that communicates with a
\f[CR]bash\-server(1)\f[R] instance over an already\-open file
descriptor.
The descriptor \f[CR]fd\f[R] must be a bidirectional (read/write) file
descriptor connected to a server that speaks the bash\-server protocol.
.PP
This transport mode is useful when:
.IP \(bu 2
A parent process has already established the connection and passes the
file descriptor to a child via \f[CR]fork(2)\f[R] or \f[CR]exec(2)\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The server was launched with \f[CR]\-\-fd N\f[R] and the client inherits
the corresponding descriptor.
.IP \(bu 2
Socket activation systems (e.g., systemd) pass pre\-connected
descriptors.
.PP
The library takes ownership of \f[CR]fd\f[R] after a successful call.
The descriptor will be closed when \f[CR]bc_close(3)\f[R] is called.
On failure, \f[CR]fd\f[R] is \f[B]not\f[R] closed \(en the caller
retains responsibility.
