.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The library takes ownership of \f[CR]fd\f[R] on success.
Do not close \f[CR]fd\f[R] directly after a successful call; use
\f[CR]bc_close(3)\f[R] instead.
.IP \(bu 2
On failure, \f[CR]fd\f[R] is not closed.
The caller must close it to avoid a file descriptor leak.
.IP \(bu 2
The descriptor must be bidirectional.
A unidirectional pipe (from \f[CR]pipe(2)\f[R]) will not work \(en use
\f[CR]bc_connect_stdio(3)\f[R] for pipe\-based communication instead.
.IP \(bu 2
The function does not validate that a bash\-server is actually listening
on the other end of \f[CR]fd\f[R].
Protocol errors will be detected on the first API call (e.g.,
\f[CR]bc_auth(3)\f[R]).
.IP \(bu 2
This function is commonly used together with the server\(cqs
\f[CR]\-\-fd\f[R] option: the parent creates a \f[CR]socketpair(2)\f[R],
passes one end to the server with \f[CR]\-\-fd\f[R], and wraps the other
end with \f[CR]bc_connect_fd\f[R].
